  "description": "Discontinued, superseded by Gen3. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic RocketMAX.\n\nYears of production: 2018-2020\n\nThe RocketMAX Gen2 was the first RocketMAX with Longshot geometry, and the first with a UK made front triangle. See the RocketMAX archive for the other generations.\n\nThe RocketMAX Gen2 was Cotic's big wheel, 29er steel full suspension enduro bike: 150mm rear travel, built around a 160mm fork.\n\nIt was the fastest bike in the range at the time, aimed squarely at the rockiest descents and steepest technical trails. Its Reynolds 853 frame carried speed through lines that would have been a fight on other bikes, with the stability and precision to stay composed on any gradient, and it still pedalled back up happily.",
